# scripts/hygiene-denylist.sha256
#
# One lowercase hex SHA-256 hash per line — never the plaintext term itself.
# scripts/hygiene-check.js lowercases scanned text, tokenizes it into words
# (`[a-z0-9]+(?:[-_][a-z0-9]+)*`), forms 2- and 3-word phrases of
# consecutive words joined by a single space, hashes each token/phrase, and
# flags a match against this list as rule `private-vocabulary (hashed)`.
#
# To add a term: compute its sha256 with
# node -e "console.log(require('crypto').createHash('sha256').update('your term here'.toLowerCase()).digest('hex'))"
# and append the hash below. Never commit the plaintext term anywhere in
# this repo (source, tests, or commit messages).
